# q2repro

q2repro is a fork of Q2PRO, which is itself a drop-in replacement for the Kex
Quake II "re-release" engine. It plays the full re-release content and is
compatible with the existing Quake II network protocols. It ships both a client
(`q2repro`) and a dedicated server (`q2reproded`), plus a game DLL
(`game_x86_64.so`) that runs inside the game directory.

Upstream: https://github.com/res2k/q2repro  (GPL-2.0-or-later)

## Build system

Meson. Build steps (same as upstream, pinned for reproducibility):

    meson setup build --prefix=/usr -Dlibdir=/usr/lib64 \
                      -Dsystem-wide=true -Dlibcurl=enabled \
                      --wrap-mode=nofallback
    meson compile -C build
    DESTDIR=$PKG meson install -C build

`--wrap-mode=nofallback` forces every optional library to come from the system
via pkg-config; no subproject is downloaded and no network access is needed at
build time. `system-wide=true` installs into `/usr` (the portable/default mode
installs into a relative `./` tree, which is not what we want here).

## Sources / git submodules

Upstream provides no release tarball that includes its two git submodules, so
this package vendors a tarball (`q2repro-<rev>.tar.xz`, git-ignored, kept next
to this SlackBuild) built with:

    git archive-style snapshot of commit <rev> + q2proto/ and
    subprojects/rerelease-game/ contents, with all .git and builddir dirs
    stripped.

`q2proto` and `rerelease-game` are required at compile time. They are NOT Meson
"wrap" subprojects, so `--wrap-mode` alone cannot fetch them; they must be
baked into the tarball. To regenerate the tarball for a new commit:

    REV=<short-sha>
    rm -rf /tmp/q2repro-src-$REV && mkdir -p /tmp/q2repro-src-$REV
    ( cd /tmp/q2repro-src-$REV && find <repo> -maxdepth 1 -mindepth 1 \
        ! -name builddir -exec cp -a {} . \; )
    for sub in q2proto subprojects/rerelease-game; do
      find /tmp/q2repro-src-$REV/$sub \( -name .git -o -name builddir \) \
        -prune -exec rm -rf {} + 2>/dev/null || true
    done
    tar -C /tmp/q2repro-src-$REV -cJf \
      games/q2repro/q2repro-$REV.tar.xz .
    md5sum games/q2repro/q2repro-$REV.tar.xz   # update MD5SUM in q2repro.info

## Dependencies

Build and runtime libraries resolved from the built binaries / meson config:

Core (Slackware full install, not listed in REQUIRES):
  zlib, libpng, libjpeg-turbo, ffmpeg (libavcodec/format/util/swresample/scale),
  libX11, libXi, wayland, wayland-protocols, libdecor, libglvnd/mesa.

SBo / other (listed in REQUIRES):
  SDL3        - video + audio backend
  OpenAL-Soft - sound backend (preferred audio path)
  jsoncpp     - pulled in by the rerelease-game DLL

Explicitly enabled:
  libcurl  - HTTP downloads. Enabled with -Dlibcurl=enabled (a hard dep now,
             since curl is installed and pkg-config resolves it, including the
             mit-krb5-gssapi entry). curl is a Slackware core package, so it is
             NOT listed in REQUIRES. With --wrap-mode=nofallback meson links the
             system libcurl rather than building the vendored curl wrap subproject.

Optional features are controlled by meson_options.txt (e.g. avcodec, libpng,
libjpeg, openal, sdl3, x11, wayland, mvd-server/mvd-client). With
`--wrap-mode=nofallback` each is enabled automatically if its system
development package is present.

## Requirements to actually run

A full (or demo) copy of Quake II, patched to 3.20. Copy the game data into the
installed game directory:

    baseq2/pak*.pak and baseq2/players  ->  /usr/lib64/q2repro/baseq2/

The client also writes config to ~/.q2repro (see the `homedir` meson option).

## Known issues / notes

- The in-binary version string is read by `version.py` from a `VERSION` file
  (written by the SlackBuild, since the vendored tarball has no .git). The
  SlackBuild hardcodes `r4625~9619f8e2`; bump the commit count/sha on rebuild.
- Man pages (docutils RST in `man/`) are converted with `rst2man` and installed
  to /usr/man/man6. If `rst2man` is missing they are skipped silently.
- `q2reproded --version` prints mapdb.json warnings when no game data is
  present; that is expected, not a build failure.

- The package filename includes ARCH (`q2repro-$VERSION-$ARCH-$BUILD.$TAG.txz`),
  e.g. `q2repro-9619f8e2-x86_64-1._vibed.txz`. Omitting ARCH breaks pkgtools'
  `package_name()` resolution of the base name, so the description would silently
  fail to record on install. Verified against /sbin/installpkg.
- The `slack-desc` is copied into `$PKG/install/` before makepkg. pkgtools reads
  `install/slack-desc` for the on-screen/stored description and removes it on
  install; a root-level `slack-desc` would instead be installed to `/slack-desc`.
